{"1-7":{"people":[{"id":"cain-h7014b","name":"Cain","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Adam","count":5,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"adam-h0121g","name":"Adam","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Cain","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"eve-h2332","name":"Eve","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"abel-h1893","name":"Abel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Adam","count":2,"firstVerse":2}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H7014","lemma":"קַ֫יִן","tr":"qa·yin","gloss":"Kain","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":19},{"base":"H1893","lemma":"הֶ֫בֶל","tr":"he·vel","gloss":"Abel","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":8},{"base":"H4503","lemma":"מִנְחָה","tr":"min·chah","gloss":"offering","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":211},{"base":"H8159","lemma":"שָׁעָה","tr":"sha·ah","gloss":"to gaze","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":15},{"base":"H2734","lemma":"חָרָה","tr":"cha·rah","gloss":"to be incensed","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":91},{"base":"H3190","lemma":"יָטַב","tr":"ya·tav","gloss":"be good","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":117},{"base":"H0127","lemma":"אֲדָמָה","tr":"a·da·mah","gloss":"land: soil","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":225},{"base":"H6629","lemma":"צֹאן","tr":"tson","gloss":"flock","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":274},{"base":"H2332","lemma":"חַוָּה","tr":"chav·vah","gloss":"Eve","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H8669","lemma":"תְּשׁוּקָה","tr":"te·shu·qah","gloss":"desire","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JAS","chapter":1,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":58,"source":"both","text":"Then after desire has conceived, it gives birth to sin; and sin, when it is full-grown, gives birth to death.","from":7},{"book":"ROM","chapter":2,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":33,"source":"openbible","text":"God “will repay each one according to his deeds.”","from":7},{"book":"ROM","chapter":2,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":33,"source":"openbible","text":"but glory, honor, and peace for everyone who does good, first for the Jew, then for the Greek.","from":7},{"book":"ISA","chapter":3,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":27,"source":"openbible","text":"Tell the righteous it will be well with them, for they will enjoy the fruit of their labor.","from":7},{"book":"ISA","chapter":3,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":27,"source":"openbible","text":"Woe to the wicked; disaster is upon them! For they will be repaid with what their hands have done.","from":7},{"book":"ROM","chapter":6,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":24,"source":"openbible","text":"Do you not know that when you offer yourselves as obedient slaves, you are slaves to the one you obey, whether you are slaves to sin leading to death, or to obedience leading to righteousness?","from":7},{"book":"HEB","chapter":11,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":24,"source":"both","text":"By faith Abel offered God a better sacrifice than Cain did. By faith he was commended as righteous when God gave approval to his gifts. And by faith he still speaks, even though he is dead.","from":4},{"book":"HEB","chapter":11,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":23,"source":"both","text":"By faith Abel offered God a better sacrifice than Cain did. By faith he was commended as righteous when God gave approval to his gifts. And by faith he still speaks, even though he is dead.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"8-12":{"people":[{"id":"abel-h1893","name":"Abel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Adam","count":2,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"cain-h7014b","name":"Cain","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Adam","count":2,"firstVerse":8}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0251","lemma":"אָח","tr":"ach","gloss":"brother: male-sibling","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":629},{"base":"H1893","lemma":"הֶ֫בֶל","tr":"he·vel","gloss":"Abel","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":8},{"base":"H7014","lemma":"קַ֫יִן","tr":"qa·yin","gloss":"Kain","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":19},{"base":"H0127","lemma":"אֲדָמָה","tr":"a·da·mah","gloss":"land: soil","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":225},{"base":"H1818","lemma":"דָּם","tr":"dam","gloss":"blood","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":360},{"base":"H6475","lemma":"פָּצָה","tr":"pa·tsah","gloss":"to open","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15},{"base":"H4480","lemma":"מִן־","tr":"min","gloss":"from","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1187},{"base":"H5110","lemma":"נוּד","tr":"nud","gloss":"to wander","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H0335","lemma":"אַי","tr":"ay","gloss":"where?","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":39},{"base":"H5128","lemma":"נוּעַ","tr":"nu·a","gloss":"to shake","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":40}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"HEB","chapter":12,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":23,"source":"both","text":"to Jesus the mediator of a new covenant, and to the sprinkled blood that speaks a better word than the blood of Abel.","from":10},{"book":"HEB","chapter":11,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"By faith Abel offered God a better sacrifice than Cain did. By faith he was commended as righteous when God gave approval to his gifts. And by faith he still speaks, even though he is dead.","from":10},{"book":"PSA","chapter":72,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"He will redeem them from oppression and violence, for their blood is precious in his sight.","from":10},{"book":"ISA","chapter":5,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"For the vineyard of the LORD of Hosts is the house of Israel, and the men of Judah are the plant of His delight. He looked for justice, but saw bloodshed; for righteousness, but heard a cry of distress.","from":10},{"book":"JAS","chapter":5,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Look, the wages you withheld from the workmen who mowed your fields are crying out against you. The cries of the harvesters have reached the ears of the Lord of Hosts.","from":10},{"book":"PSA","chapter":9,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"For the Avenger of bloodshed remembers; He does not ignore the cry of the afflicted.","from":10},{"book":"PRO","chapter":28,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"He who conceals his sins will not prosper, but whoever confesses and renounces them will find mercy.","from":9},{"book":"MAT","chapter":23,"verse":35,"verseEnd":35,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"And so upon you will come all the righteous blood shed on earth, from the blood of righteous Abel to the blood of Zechariah son of Berechiah, whom you murdered between the temple and the altar.","from":8}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"13-16":{"people":[{"id":"cain-h7014b","name":"Cain","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Adam","count":3,"firstVerse":13}],"places":[{"id":"eden-h5731b","name":"Eden","kind":"place","brief":"In Mesopotamia","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"nod-h5113","name":"Nod","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":16}],"words":[{"base":"H7014","lemma":"קַ֫יִן","tr":"qa·yin","gloss":"Kain","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":19},{"base":"H2026","lemma":"הָרַג","tr":"ha·rag","gloss":"to kill","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":167},{"base":"H4672","lemma":"מָצָא","tr":"ma·tsa","gloss":"to find","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":455},{"base":"H6926","lemma":"קִדְמָה","tr":"qid·mah","gloss":"east","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H7659","lemma":"שִׁבְעָתַיִם","tr":"shiv·a·ta·yim","gloss":"sevenfold","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H5731","lemma":"עֵ֫דֶן","tr":"e·den","gloss":"Eden","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H5110","lemma":"נוּד","tr":"nud","gloss":"to wander","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H5358","lemma":"נָקַם","tr":"na·qam","gloss":"to avenge","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":35},{"base":"H5128","lemma":"נוּעַ","tr":"nu·a","gloss":"to shake","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":40},{"base":"H1644","lemma":"גָּרַשׁ","tr":"ga·rash","gloss":"to drive out: drive out","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":47}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NUM","chapter":35,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The avenger of blood is to put the murderer to death; when he finds him, he is to kill him.","from":14},{"book":"EZK","chapter":9,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"“Go throughout the city of Jerusalem,” said the LORD, “and put a mark on the foreheads of the men sighing and groaning over all the abominations committed there.”","from":15},{"book":"JOB","chapter":15,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"A wicked man writhes in pain all his days; only a few years are reserved for the ruthless.","from":14},{"book":"JOB","chapter":15,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"He despairs of his return from darkness; he is marked for the sword.","from":13},{"book":"JOB","chapter":15,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Distress and anguish terrify him, overwhelming him like a king poised to attack.","from":14},{"book":"PSA","chapter":79,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Pay back into the laps of our neighbors sevenfold the reproach they hurled at You, O Lord.","from":15},{"book":"PSA","chapter":143,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Answer me quickly, O LORD; my spirit fails. Do not hide Your face from me, or I will be like those who descend to the Pit.","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the man and his wife heard the voice of the LordGod walking in the garden in the breeze of the day, and they hid themselves from the presence of the LordGod among the trees of the garden.","from":16}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"17-24":{"people":[{"id":"cain-h7014b","name":"Cain","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Adam","count":2,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"enoch-h2585g","name":"Enoch","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Cain","count":2,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"lamech-h3929g","name":"Lamech","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Methushael","count":4,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"irad-h5897","name":"Irad","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Enoch","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"mehujael-h4232","name":"Mehujael","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Irad","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"methushael-h4967","name":"Methushael","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Mehujael","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"adah-h5711g","name":"Adah","kind":"person","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"zillah-h6741","name":"Zillah","kind":"person","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"jabal-h2989","name":"Jabal","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Lamech","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"jubal-h3106","name":"Jubal","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Lamech","count":1,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"naamah-h5279g","name":"Naamah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Jabal","count":1,"firstVerse":22},{"id":"tubal-cain-h8423","name":"Tubal-cain","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Lamech","count":1,"firstVerse":22}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3929","lemma":"לֶ֫מֶךְ","tr":"le·mekh","gloss":"Lamech","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":11},{"base":"H8423","lemma":"תּוּבַל־קַ֫יִן","tr":"tu·val qa·yin","gloss":"Tubal-cain","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":4},{"base":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","tr":"ya·lad","gloss":"to beget","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":496},{"base":"H6741","lemma":"צִלָּה","tr":"tsil·lah","gloss":"Zillah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":3},{"base":"H5711","lemma":"עָדָה","tr":"a·dah","gloss":"Adah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":8},{"base":"H2585","lemma":"חֲנוֹךְ","tr":"cha·nokh","gloss":"Enoch","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":16},{"base":"H8034","lemma":"שֵׁם","tr":"shem","gloss":"name","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":864},{"base":"H4232","lemma":"מְחוּיָאֵל","tr":"me·chu·ya·el","gloss":"Mehujael","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H4967","lemma":"מְתוּשָׁאֵל","tr":"me·tu·sha·el","gloss":"Methushael","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H5897","lemma":"עִירָד","tr":"i·rad","gloss":"Irad","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"MAT","chapter":18,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Jesus answered, “I tell you, not just seven times, but seventy-seven times!","from":24},{"book":"GEN","chapter":4,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"“Not so!” replied the Lord. “If anyone slays Cain, then Cain will be avenged sevenfold.” And the Lordplaced a mark on Cain, so that no one who found him would kill him.","from":24},{"book":"GEN","chapter":2,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The LordGod also said, “It is not good for the man to be alone. I will make for him a suitable helper.”","from":19},{"book":"GEN","chapter":2,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and they will become one flesh.","from":19},{"book":"GEN","chapter":4,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Later she gave birth to Cainʼs brother Abel. Now Abel was a keeper of sheep, while Cain was a tiller of the soil.","from":20},{"book":"GEN","chapter":5,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Jared was 162 years old, he became the father of Enoch.","from":17},{"book":"GEN","chapter":5,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When Enoch was 65 years old, he became the father of Methuselah.","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":5,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And after he had become the father of Methuselah, Enoch walked with God 300 years and had other sons and daughters.","from":17}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"25-26":{"people":[{"id":"seth-h8352","name":"Seth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Adam","count":2,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"abel-h1893","name":"Abel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Adam","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"adam-h0121g","name":"Adam","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Cain","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"cain-h7014b","name":"Cain","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Adam","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"enosh-h0583","name":"Enosh","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Seth","count":1,"firstVerse":26}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H8352","lemma":"שֵׁת","tr":"shet","gloss":"Seth","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":9},{"base":"H7121","lemma":"קָרָא","tr":"qa·ra","gloss":"to call: call to","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":733},{"base":"H8034","lemma":"שֵׁם","tr":"shem","gloss":"name","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":864},{"base":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","tr":"ya·lad","gloss":"to beget","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":496},{"base":"H0583","lemma":"אֱנוֹשׁ","tr":"e·nosh","gloss":"Enosh","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H1893","lemma":"הֶ֫בֶל","tr":"he·vel","gloss":"Abel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H0121","lemma":"אָדָם","tr":"a·dam","gloss":"Adam","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H7014","lemma":"קַ֫יִן","tr":"qa·yin","gloss":"Kain","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":19},{"base":"H7896","lemma":"שִׁית","tr":"shit","gloss":"to set: make","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":83},{"base":"H0227","lemma":"אָז","tr":"az","gloss":"then","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":141}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":116,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"I will offer to You a sacrifice of thanksgiving and call on the name of the LORD.","from":26},{"book":"1KI","chapter":18,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Then you may call on the name of your god, and I will call on the name of the LORD. The God who answers by fire, He is God.” And all the people answered, “What you say is good.”","from":26},{"book":"JOL","chapter":2,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"And everyone who calls on the name of the LORD will be saved; for on Mount Zion and in Jerusalem there will be deliverance, as the LORD has promised, among the remnant called by the LORD.","from":26},{"book":"ZEP","chapter":3,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"For then I will restore pure lips to the peoples, that all may call upon the name of the LORD and serve Him shoulder to shoulder.","from":26},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"From there Abram moved on to the hill country east of Bethel and pitched his tent, with Bethel to the west and Ai to the east. There he built an altar to the Lord, and he called on the name of the Lord.","from":26},{"book":"GEN","chapter":26,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"So Isaac built an altar there and called on the name of the Lord, and he pitched his tent there. His servants also dug a well there.","from":26},{"book":"JER","chapter":33,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"In those days Judah will be saved, and Jerusalem will dwell securely, and this is the name by which it will be called: The LORD Our Righteousness.","from":26},{"book":"LUK","chapter":3,"verse":38,"verseEnd":38,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"the son of Enosh, the son of Seth, the son of Adam, the son of God.","from":26}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}